{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109478-diablerie-questions","id":1109478,"title":"diablerie questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-29T16:57:02-07:00","id":1109478,"title":"diablerie questions","content":"is there a merit or cruic or coil that lets you hide it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T17:02:31-07:00","id":1109480,"title":"","content":"Nope.<br /> <br /> Only thing I remember that can hide Diablerie stains is the En Bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T17:42:40-07:00","id":1109503,"title":"","content":"There's the Carthian Law in second edition that hides it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T17:44:25-07:00","id":1109504,"title":"","content":"If there isn't one you definitely can make it, best thing about this system is its flexibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T20:26:55-07:00","id":1109573,"title":"","content":"Active Obfuscate 1 can conceal diablerie stains but it can be overcome. Love Lies Bleeding, a Cruac ritual hides diablerie stains. Plausible Deniability, a Carthian Law merit hides diablerie stains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T21:10:24-07:00","id":1109589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109478-diablerie-questions?p=1109573#post1109573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Active Obfuscate 1 can conceal diablerie stains but it can be overcome. Love Lies Bleeding, a Cruac ritual hides diablerie stains. Plausible Deniability, a Carthian Law merit hides diablerie stains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when did Obfuscate 1 hide diablerie stains? I've never noticed anything about that in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T23:09:44-07:00","id":1109638,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate hides the whole vampire so that would count as hiding the taint of diablerie. It isn't like someone could search for diablerie specifically without overcoming Obfuscate to find the vampire, at best they would get a general location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T00:19:02-07:00","id":1109645,"title":"","content":"I don't think it is what princepfcincinnati had in mind. I think he want know if there is a way, for a diablerist, to interact with other kindred hiding the taint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T05:41:31-07:00","id":1109709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109478-diablerie-questions?p=1109589#post1109589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since when did Obfuscate 1 hide diablerie stains? I've never noticed anything about that in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate 1 hides the individual user's predatory aura. It's right there in the description. The power also makes them nonspecific in a crowd. Detecting diablerie entails scanning a single target's aura. As Diggs pointed out, you can't scan the aura of someone you can't pinpoint. Attempting a question to the effect of &quot;who in the area is a diablerist&quot; is going to engender a clash of wills with the Obfuscate user being the defender if they have Obfuscate 1 active.<br /> It hides diablerie but it can be overcome. The other two powers are incontravertible unless you have a blood sympathy to the victim, an in-game way to strip away protective spells on someone or the ability to shut down Carthian Law, or managed to finagle an Invictus Oath on the diablerist where the wannabe diablerie detector is the liege and the diablerist is the vassal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-30-2017, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T17:58:16-07:00","id":1109982,"title":"","content":"Well, no context was provided. If there is some specific test that must be overcome then that needs to be detailed. Obfuscate 1 makes someone unremarkable, not noticed or not remembered. As long as one doesn't make a scene and there is no Clash, there are no limits to interacting with others. People will likely forget after, but memorable interaction was given as a requirement while hiding. It is common practice for powers without &quot;friendly fire&quot; issues to be selective and only partially effective, especially when they already are. So it isn't in the book that you can use Obfuscate 1 just to hide diablerie taint, but I would allow it if the other aspects were undesirable with the same limitations on the power that it normally has, as I would if a vampire was only trying to hide a vampiric nature. It is a risky way to hide the taint to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T19:56:32-07:00","id":1110020,"title":"","content":"I had the character make a bargain with one of the Fae. He now has a ring (token) that makes him look sparkling clean. of course there was a deal made. The Fae took one dot of intelligence from him and his memories of the last month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}